  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Let $K=MN.$ What is the value of ${k}_{12}$, if\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,N=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -5\\end{aligned}]?\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Multiplying the $1$st row in $M$ by the $2$nd column in $N$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{k}_{12} & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-1)+(-4)\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-5+8 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
